    {
      "id": "tectonics-detail",
      "type": "face",
      "label": "The idea explained",
      "position": {
        "x": -1100,
        "y": 1233
      },
      "width": 450,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tectonics-demo"
        },
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail",
          "scroll": "page"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:#fffaf5;font-family:Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;min-height:100%;padding:4.4cqw 7cqw 5cqw'><div style='font:700 1.3cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c2410c'>Idea map</div><div style='font:700 5.2cqw/1.12 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#1f2937'>Plate tectonics</div><div style='font:400 2.1cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:2cqw;max-width:62cqw'>Earth&#39;s outer shell is broken into moving plates, and almost everything about the planet&#39;s surface follows from that.</div><div style='margin-top:1.6cqw;font:600 1.6cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;color:#64748b'>6 points · 1 of 1 question open</div><div style='font:700 1.3cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c2410c;margin:4cqw 0 1.6cqw;padding-top:2cqw;border-top:.15cqw solid rgba(194,65,12,.35)'>The idea, explained</div><div style='margin:0 0 2cqw 0cqw;padding:1.8cqw 2.2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:.6cqw solid #0369a1'><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:.5cqw'>is made of</div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;align-items:baseline'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>The lithosphere</div><div style='flex:0 0 auto'><span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 1.3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#0369a1;border:1px solid #0369a1'>Part</span></div></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>The rigid outer layer, about 100 km thick, is cracked into around a dozen major plates.</div></div><div style='margin:0 0 2cqw 3.2cqw;padding:1.8cqw 2.2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:.6cqw solid #15803d'><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:.5cqw'>is moved by</div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;align-items:baseline'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>The mantle moves</div><div style='flex:0 0 auto'><span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 1.3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#15803d;border:1px solid #15803d'>Reason</span></div></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Slow convection in the hot mantle below drags the plates along, a few centimetres a year.</div><div style='margin-top:.9cqw;padding:1cqw 1.6cqw;border-radius:1cqw;background:#faf5ff;border:1px solid #e9d5ff;font:italic 1.6cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#7e22ce'>Still unsure: <b style='font-style:normal'>Why do plates move?</b> <span style='color:#334155'>Is it mantle convection, slab pull or ridge push? Scientists still weigh the three.</span></div></div><div style='margin:0 0 2cqw 0cqw;padding:1.8cqw 2.2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:.6cqw solid #0369a1'><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:.5cqw'>shows up at</div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;align-items:baseline'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Plate boundaries</div><div style='flex:0 0 auto'><span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 1.3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#0369a1;border:1px solid #0369a1'>Part</span></div></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Plates diverge, converge or slide past each other, and each kind builds something different.</div></div><div style='margin:0 0 2cqw 3.2cqw;padding:1.8cqw 2.2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:.6cqw solid #c2410c'><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:.5cqw'>causes</div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;align-items:baseline'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Earthquakes and volcanoes</div><div style='flex:0 0 auto'><span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 1.3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#c2410c;border:1px solid #c2410c'>Example</span></div></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>They cluster along boundaries, where plates grind, sink and melt.</div></div><div style='margin:0 0 2cqw 3.2cqw;padding:1.8cqw 2.2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:.6cqw solid #b91c1c'><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:.5cqw'>but</div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;align-items:baseline'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Quakes far from any boundary</div><div style='flex:0 0 auto'><span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 1.3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#b91c1c;border:1px solid #b91c1c'>Objection</span></div></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Some earthquakes happen deep inside plates, which the boundary picture does not explain on its own.</div></div><div style='margin:0 0 2cqw 0cqw;padding:1.8cqw 2.2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:.6cqw solid #c2410c'><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:.5cqw'>explains</div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;align-items:baseline'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Continental drift</div><div style='flex:0 0 auto'><span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 1.3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#c2410c;border:1px solid #c2410c'>Example</span></div></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Matching coastlines and fossils suggested the continents were once joined. Plate tectonics explained how.</div></div><div style='font:700 1.3cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c2410c;margin:4cqw 0 1.6cqw;padding-top:2cqw;border-top:.15cqw solid rgba(194,65,12,.35)'>Still open</div><div style='margin-bottom:1.4cqw'><div style='font:700 1.8cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#7e22ce'>Why do plates move?</div><div style='font:600 1.3cqw/1.5 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;color:#64748b'>Raised by The mantle moves</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Is it mantle convection, slab pull or ridge push? Scientists still weigh the three.</div></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Detail: the idea explained, walked outward from the centre, written from the cards. The Method writes it, so edit the cards and not this.",
